Tools, Technologies, and Architectures for Real-Time Data Pipelines
Tools:

Apache Kafka: Distributed messaging and streaming platform.
Apache Flink: Stream processing framework for stateful computations.
Google Dataflow: Fully managed stream and batch data processing service.
AWS Kinesis: Real-time data streaming service.
Apache Spark (Structured Streaming): Unified engine for batch and real-time data processing.
ElasticSearch: For real-time search and analytics.
PostgreSQL: As a database for storing processed data.
MinIO: High-performance, S3-compatible object storage.
Superset: For data visualization.
Architectures:

Lambda Architecture: Combines batch and real-time processing.
Kappa Architecture: Designed for stream processing only.
Event-Driven Architecture: Systems react to events in real-time using event logs or message queues.
Lakehouse Architecture: Combines data lakes and warehousing (e.g., using Iceberg, Delta Lake).

